// Default Zed settings for aetherion zed-ide namespaces.
//
// This file is a *seed* (skeleton dotfile per STYLE.md): copied into
// the namespace's $HOME on first launch and frozen there. Edits the
// user makes inside the namespace win; rebuilding the image does NOT
// refresh this file (use `aetherion reset namespace <name>` if you
// want to drop user changes and reseed).
//
// Zed reads ~/.config/zed/settings.json on Linux (XDG). Project-level
// overrides at <project>/.zed/settings.json still apply on top.
//
// Intentional defaults below — everything else is left at Zed's
// upstream defaults so the editor feels like vanilla Zed:
//
//   - title_bar.show_sign_in: false
//       Hides the top-right "Sign in" button. The container has no
//       persistent Zed-account session anyway and the button just
//       distracts. Users who want Zed AI / collab features can flip
//       this back to `true` per-namespace.
//
//   - telemetry.diagnostics: false
//   - telemetry.metrics: false
//       Aetherion namespaces are ephemeral build sandboxes — crash
//       reports and usage pings from inside one don't represent real
//       user environments and would just be noise to Zed Industries.
//       Opt back in per-namespace if you want to send them.
//
//   - auto_update: false
//       Image-managed install at /opt/zed.app. In-namespace updates
//       would land in $HOME and be lost on `aetherion rebuild
//       namespace`. To refresh, rebuild the image with a newer
//       ZED_VERSION build arg.
//
//   - project_panel.dock: "left"
//       File tree on the left (Zed defaults to "right"). Sole left
//       dweller, so it doesn't fight anything for the slot.
//
//   - agent.dock: "right"
//   - agent.sidebar_side: "right"
//       Agent / threads / chat panel on the right (Zed defaults to
//       "left"). With project_panel on the left, this gives a
//       three-column layout: files | editor | chat. The inner
//       sidebar (thread/history list) also pins right so the chat
//       textarea hugs the editor and the thread list hugs the window
//       edge.
//
//   - git_panel.dock: "right"
//   - outline_panel.dock: "right"
//       Everything that isn't the file tree groups onto the right
//       dock — single mental model for "where do non-file panels
//       live" and avoids the default left-dock pileup with the file
//       tree.
//
// NOT settable today: auto-opening the agent panel on first launch.
// Only project_panel has a `starts_open` key (see Zed issue #51542
// — tracking parity for the other dock panels). Open it once with
// `cmd-?` / `ctrl-?` and Zed's default `restore_on_startup:
// "last_session"` will reopen it on subsequent launches into the
// same namespace.
{
  "title_bar": {
    "show_sign_in": false,
  },
  "telemetry": {
    "diagnostics": false,
    "metrics": false,
  },
  "auto_update": false,
  "project_panel": { "dock": "left" },
  "agent": {
    "dock": "right",
    "sidebar_side": "right",
  },
  "git_panel": { "dock": "right" },
  "outline_panel": { "dock": "right" },
}
